        "original_id": "544b28a4-8950-5fab-a999-685ec791c738",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eagle Feather, Jim Thorpe, Eddie Mahan\n- Organizations: Indians, Sac and Fox Nation\n- Places: LaRue, Ohio\n- Topics: Native American athletes, football\n\nFacts:\n- The Indians were a team based in LaRue, Ohio, composed only of Native Americans, and Eagle Feather played for the team.\n- Jim Thorpe coached the Indians team in LaRue, Ohio.\n- Jim Thorpe was a member of the Sac and Fox Nation.\n- Jim Thorpe became the first Native American to win a gold medal for his home country.\n- Eddie Mahan was widely regarded as one of the greatest football players in the first 50 years of the sport.\n- Jim Thorpe named Eddie Mahan the greatest football player of all time.",
